 "summary": "The ModuleCat principal d\u00e9calage over a general f is new material, and the f = p case is linked to the existing CR.4 `normalizedDecalage` by `forget\u2082PrincipalDecalageIso` rather than reproved, as the roadmap prescribes. `isSMulRegular_natCast_iff` now reuses `Equiv.isSMulRegular_congr`; it is a \u2115-base specialization of Mathlib's `isSMulRegular_algebraMap_iff` (Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Basic.lean:411), but using that lemma would need an algebraMap-to-cast rewrite and the lemma has consumers in this PR, so it is not a finding.",
